-- LookupResult — the explicit-ambiguity surface for `dispatch.lookup`
-- (Phase 10a sub-step 1). Callers pattern-match each arm rather than letting
-- the registry silently "highest priority wins". `Unique` carries the single
-- match; `Conflict` the multi-candidate list; `None` the empty result.
--
-- FM-retire-E1 Step 7 — the inline `defineSystemEntity({ codeName:
-- "LookupResult", … })` is DELETED; this decl is the catalog-facing source.
-- The `LookupResult(a)` builder in `type-foundation.ts` STAYS the dispatch-side
-- producer (it sidesteps the foundation-loader TDZ window Maybe/Result/Either
-- have to manage) — this file mirrors its shape byte-for-byte: named fields
-- `Unique value: a` / `Conflict items: List a`, matching the helper's output.
-- The head param `a` flows onto the registered entity's `params` via the
-- loader's Step-7 head-param threading (registers as `{$var:"a"}`, the
-- canonical type-var form — the pre-flip TS literal used the arbitrary name
-- `A`, so the oracle re-pins the name; the handle is unchanged).

@entity
@label "Lookup Result"
@icon "split"
@description "Explicit-ambiguity surface for dispatch.lookup — Unique a | Conflict (List a) | None. Callers explicitly handle each arm rather than the registry silently picking. Phase 10a sub-step 1 only populates Unique / None; Conflict becomes load-bearing once 10a-4's typed-Id dispatch makes duplicate registrations structurally detectable."
LookupResult a = Unique value: a | Conflict items: List a | None
